{"book": "gate-da", "num": 22, "label": "22", "slug": "22-calculus-continuity", "title": "Continuity", "tag": "Calculus & Optimization", "summary": "A function $f(x)$ is continuous at a point $a$ if the following three conditions hold:", "wordCount": 238, "readingTimeMin": 1, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "22.1", "title": "Continuity of Functions", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Continuity at a Point", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A function $f(x)$ is <b>continuous at a point $a$</b> if the following three conditions hold:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$f(a)$ is defined."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)$ exists."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = f(a)$."}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "If any condition fails, $f$ is <b>discontinuous</b> at $a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Procedure to Check Continuity", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Verify that $f(a)$ exists."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Compute $\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)$, including left- and right-hand limits if needed."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Compare $f(a)$ with the limit. Equality confirms continuity."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "75", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Continuity at a Point}\nDetermine if $f(x) = \\frac{x^2-1}{x-1}$ is continuous at $x=1$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n$f(1)$ is undefined since denominator $x-1=0$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion:</b> $f$ is discontinuous at $x=1$ (removable discontinuity)."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "76", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Continuity at a Point}\nDetermine if"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(x) = \n\\begin{cases} \nx^2, & x \\neq 2 \\\\\n5, & x = 2\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "is continuous at $x=2$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\n$\\lim_{x \\to 2} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to 2} x^2 = 4$.\n$f(2) = 5 \\neq 4$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion:</b> $f$ is discontinuous at $x=2$ (removable discontinuity)."}]}]}, {"id": "22.2", "title": "Types of Discontinuities", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Classification", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Removable:</b> Limit exists but $f(a) \\neq \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Jump:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) \\neq \\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Infinite:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = \\pm \\infty$ or $\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = \\pm \\infty$."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Graphical Representation", "blocks": [{"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/calc/fig026.png"], "caption": ""}]}]}, {"id": "22.3", "title": "Continuity over an Interval", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Continuity on Intervals", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous from right at $a$:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = f(a)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous from left at $a$:</b> $\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = f(a)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous on $(a,b)$:</b> Continuous at every point in $(a,b)$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuous on $[a,b]$:</b> Continuous on $(a,b)$, right-continuous at $a$, left-continuous at $b$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "77", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Continuity on Interval}\nFind intervals of continuity for $f(x) = \\frac{x+2}{x^2-1}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nDenominator zero when $x^2-1 = 0 \\implies x = \\pm 1$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Answer:</b> $(-\\infty,-1) \\cup (-1,1) \\cup (1,\\infty)$"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "78", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Continuity on Interval}\nFind intervals of continuity for $f(x) = \\sqrt{9-x^2}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nInside square root $\\ge 0 \\implies 9-x^2 \\ge 0 \\implies -3 \\le x \\le 3$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Answer:</b> $[-3,3]$"}]}]}, {"id": "22.4", "title": "Composite Functions and Trigonometric Continuity", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Composite Function Theorem", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $L$ and $\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x) = L$, then"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(g(x)) = f\\left(\\lim_{x \\to a} g(x)\\right) = f(L)"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "79", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Limit of a Composite Function}\nEvaluate $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\sin(3x)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nLet $g(x)=3x$, $\\lim_{x\\to 0} g(x)=0$, and $\\sin$ is continuous at 0."}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\sin(3x) = \\sin(0) = 0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Continuity of Trigonometric Functions", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\sin x$, $\\cos x$, $\\tan x$, $\\cot x$, $\\sec x$, $\\csc x$ are continuous on their domains."}]}]}, {"id": "22.5", "title": "Intermediate Value Theorem (IVT)", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Intermediate Value Theorem", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and $z$ lies between $f(a)$ and $f(b)$, then $\\exists c \\in (a,b)$ such that $f(c)=z$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "80", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Application of IVT}\nShow that $f(x) = x^3 - x - 2$ has a root in $[1,2]$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(1) = 1 -1 -2 = -2 < 0, \\quad f(2) = 8 -2 -2 = 4 >0"}, {"t": "p", "x": "$f$ is continuous (polynomial). By IVT, $\\exists c \\in (1,2)$ with $f(c)=0$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "81", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Root Existence Using IVT}\nShow that $f(x) = \\cos x - x$ has a root in $[0,1]$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f(0) = 1 - 0 = 1 > 0, \\quad f(1) = \\cos 1 -1 \\approx 0.5403 -1 = -0.4597 <0"}, {"t": "p", "x": "$f$ is continuous (trig function). IVT guarantees $\\exists c \\in (0,1)$ with $f(c)=0$."}]}]}], "sectionCount": 5}